**How to implement.** The view-only Edit gating of the domain-free materials control is deleted, with nothing replacing it (.spec-md §3.2). Its stated purpose was the `complexity = None` built-ins (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/MaterialsControls.fs:27-29`), and no product view hosts the control: `materialsControlsView` is mounted only by `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs:154` and `:190`. The Materials window keeps its own gate, `MaterialsWindowModel.editableSelection` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs:258-264`), which reads `MaterialComplexity.isEditable`. (1) `MaterialsControls.fs`: delete `MaterialEditability` (`:32-36`) and `MaterialsControlsRow.editability` (`:44`). `verbRow` (`:213-235`) always lists the Edit verb, offered on a selection exactly as Remove and View are. The module doc's view-only sentences (`:27-29`) and `verbRow`'s doc clause on Edit (`:213-215`) are deleted. The verb row's membership no longer changes, so `verbButton` drops `withKey` and its comment (`:157-159`). (2) `MaterialsControlsTests.fs`: `knownRows` (`:26-33`) lose `editability`, and their doc loses the view-only row; `matchesId`'s doc (`:20-22`) loses the Edit-removal example. The fact `a view-only selection carries no Edit affordance — the button is removed, not greyed` (`:183-201`) becomes `every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial`: with the silicon row selected, the Edit verb MUST be present and a click on it MUST record the edit handler's tag, as `recorder` (`:60`) records the others.

**Acceptance.** After the gating is deleted, ui-smoke MUST pass with `every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial` in place of the view-only fact; ui-tests (MaterialsControlsTests) MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.
